  - domain-extraction
  - unsupervised-learning
  - bioinformatics
license: MIT
abstract: |
  We demonstrate that averaging mid-to-late transformer layers (20-33) in ESM-2
  outperforms the standard final-layer approach by 32% for kinase functional
  classification. This finding generalizes beyond kinases and suggests that layer
  selection should be a standard consideration for any protein language model
  application. We provide homology-aware evaluation at multiple identity thresholds
  (70%, 50%, 40%), calibrated uncertainty quantification, and comprehensive baselines.
  All code, data, and trained models are publicly available.
